MLE for linear regression in matrix form
\[
\begin{aligned}
L(\boldsymbol{\beta}, \sigma^2_{\epsilon} | \mathbf{X}, \mathbf{y}) &= (2\pi)^{-n/2}|\sigma^2_\epsilon \mathbf{I}|^{-1/2}\exp\Big\{-\frac{1}{2}(\mathbf{y} - \mathbf{X}\boldsymbol{\beta})^\mathsf{T}(\sigma^2_{\epsilon}\mathbf{I})^{-1}(\mathbf{y} - \mathbf{X}\boldsymbol{\beta})\Big\} \\[8pt]
& = \frac{1}{(2\pi)^{n/2}\sigma^n_{\epsilon}}\exp\Big\{-\frac{1}{2\sigma^2_{\epsilon}}(\mathbf{y} - \mathbf{X}\boldsymbol{\beta})^\mathsf{T}(\mathbf{y} - \mathbf{X}\boldsymbol{\beta})\Big\}
\end{aligned}
\] 

\[
\begin{aligned}
\log L(\boldsymbol{\beta}, \sigma^2_\epsilon &| \mathbf{X}, \mathbf{y}) \\
& = -\frac{n}{2}\log(2\pi) - n \log(\sigma_{\epsilon}) - \frac{1}{2\sigma^2_{\epsilon}}(\mathbf{y} - \mathbf{X}\boldsymbol{\beta})^\mathsf{T}(\mathbf{y} - \mathbf{X}\mathbf{\beta})
\end{aligned}
\]




